# muOS Anbernic Manager

Local web app for MustardOS handhelds: Node 23.6+ server in `src/` (TypeScript run directly, no build) and a
plain ES-module front end in `public/`, served on 127.0.0.1 with a per-run token.

## Find things fast

- Module map, request flow, device paths: `docs/architecture.md` (read it before scanning the tree).
- Each file's first comment says what it does: `rg -n "^// " src/games/library.ts`.
- API routes: the `routes` object in `src/server.ts` (`rg -n '"(GET|POST|PUT|DELETE) /api/' src/server.ts`).
- Front-end entry: `public/js/app.js`; helpers and the API client: `public/js/core.js`.
- User docs: `public/js/wiki.js` (`ARTICLES`), `README.md`.

Do not read `node_modules/`, `.cache/` or the user's `Roms/`, `os/`, `apps/` folders (large, private).

## After every change

```bash
npm run check && npm test
node --check public/js/<changed>.js
LC_ALL=C rg -n '[^\x00-\x7F]' <changed files>   # must print nothing for new lines
```

## Style

- Match the surrounding code: small functions, early returns, no needless abstraction.
- Comments only state a constraint the code cannot show; no "what the next line does" comments.
- User-facing strings are plain, friendly sentences; errors say what to do next.
- Feature changes update their test, the wiki article and, when users notice, the README.
